the vaccine rollout continues  but now with a reality check the medical  regulator has revealed two health  workers had allergic reactions after  receiving the jab on tuesday  both had a medical history of  significant allergic problems  and are recovering well thousands of  people have been immunized without any  issues  jazz a care home manager nearly died of  kobit  he's relieved to return to the  gloucester royal hospital for the  vaccine  this is only the beginning and i don't  think this should replace things that we  have  in place but i think this is another  layer of how we can protect ourselves  and each other  and i just implore people to to think  really hard and just to do it for all  the right  reasons they are going to be doubters  but i think we should do it  the mhra is investigating both cases  they're understood to have suffered an  anaphylactoid reaction  which can cause breathlessness and skin  rashes rather than a life-threatening  anaphylaxis  as a precaution it's advising that for  the time being people with a significant  medical history of reacting to vaccines  medicines or food  should not have the new jab we know from  the  very extensive clinical trials that this  wasn't a feature  but if we need to strengthen our advice  now that we've had this experience  in the vulnerable populations the groups  who've been selected as a priority  we get that advice to the field  immediately  according to pfizer more than 44 000  people have been involved in clinical  trials  six in every one thousand had an  allergic reaction to the vaccine  but five in every one thousand had a  reaction to the harmless placebo jab  so any extra risk from the vaccine seems  to be relatively small  both pfizer and biontech are working  with the mhra to understand the cause of  the reactions  this former medicines regulator said all  drugs even routine painkillers have  risks  there will be things that will be  genuine adverse reactions  and we need to bear  the balance of the benefit from having  the vaccination  with a very small chance of the risk the  problem is of course  you can't find the person whose death  was prevented  you find the person who got the  anaphylactoid reaction and so you can  get it out of proportion  just relax your arm down for me thank  you all the evidence points to the  vaccine being safe  canada has become the second country to  approve its use  meanwhile margaret keenan who was the  first person to receive it in the  rollout  has left hospital a hero after a day in  the limelight she's looking forward to  celebrating her 91st  birthday next week  thomas more sky news
 

